    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "For the usage of `.includes` we should make a choice. Either we consider it as available (via polyfill when it's not) then we use it everywhere and we drop the usage of `lodash/includes`. Or we don't use this feature until it's widely supported and we keep using the lodash version. WDYT?",
    "commit_id": "2fbc55f88119929b15bbb561b92c3d96ac15eedf",
    "created_at": "2018-07-02T13:24:22Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -117,7 +117,9 @@ Start by [adding widgets](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/v2/widg\n \n ## Browser support\n \n-We support the last **two versions of major browsers**. To support [IE11](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Explorer_11), we recommend using [polyfill.io](https://polyfill.io).\n+We support the last **two versions of major browsers** (Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari).\n+\n+To support [IE11](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Explorer_11), we recommend loading [polyfill.io](https://polyfill.io) with the following URL `https://cdn.polyfill.io/v2/polyfill.min.js?features=default,Array.prototype.includes`",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/pull/3021#discussion_r199495305",
    "id": 199495305,
